flowchart TB
    accTitle: AI query assistant — decide, query, and explain
    accDescr: Follow the numbered connectors. Subnumbers identify branches or smaller steps. Optional actions and supporting relationships are labeled separately. The assistant can answer directly or use the connected database. For a data question it drafts SQL from the question and table list, checks the query, executes exactly the checked SQL with read-only access, and optionally explains all loaded rows, up to 1,000. Query errors fail the turn, while an explanation-only failure can preserve the table.
    %% Companion guide: docs/query-agent.md

    QUESTION["Read the question and recent conversation"]:::work
    NEEDS{"Does the answer need database data?"}:::work
    DIRECT["Answer directly"]:::work
    SQL["Draft SQL using the table and column list"]:::work
    CHECK["Check that the query is allowed"]:::work
    RUN["Run that exact query with read-only access"]:::data
    SUMMARY["Optionally explain all loaded rows"]:::work
    FINAL["Finish: Send the final answer with a table when available"]:::view
    ERROR["If generation or querying fails: Return a clear error"]:::note
    WARNING["If only the explanation fails: Keep the table with a warning"]:::note

    QUESTION -->|1| NEEDS
    NEEDS -->|2.a. No| DIRECT
    DIRECT -->|3.a. Direct answer| FINAL
    NEEDS -->|2.b. Yes| SQL
    SQL -->|3.b| CHECK
    CHECK -->|4| RUN
    RUN -->|5| SUMMARY
    SUMMARY -->|6| FINAL
    RUN -.->|On error| ERROR
    SQL -.->|On error| ERROR
    CHECK -.->|On error| ERROR
    SUMMARY -.->|Explanation fails| WARNING

    classDef view fill:#eff6ff,stroke:#2563eb,color:#172033,stroke-width:1.5px;
    classDef work fill:#f5f3ff,stroke:#7c3aed,color:#4c1d95,stroke-width:1.5px;
    classDef data fill:#ecfdf5,stroke:#059669,color:#064e3b,stroke-width:1.5px;
    classDef note fill:#fffbeb,stroke:#d97706,color:#78350f,stroke-width:1.5px;
